    "encrypted": "false",
    "display_name": "Using RGB Colors",
    "long_instructions": "# Using RGB\r\n\r\nExperiment with the RGB values in the CSS style sheet. \r\n\r\n# Do This\r\n1) Find the CSS rule-set in the style sheet that gives the h1 tag its style. Change *only* the first 0 to 255.\r\n* Find the CSS rule-set in the style sheet that gives the p tag its style. Change *only* the second 0 to 255.\r\n* Find the CSS rule-set in the style sheet that gives the h3 tag its style. Change *only* the third 0 to 255.\r\n\r\n::: details [🔎 **Show Me How** 🔍]\r\n\r\n```\r\nh1 {\r\n  color: rgb( 255 , 0, 0);\r\n}\r\nh3 {\r\n  color: rgb( 0 , 0 , 255);\r\n}\r\np {\r\n  color: rgb( 0 , 255, 0);\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n**More resources are in the \"Help and Tips\" tab**\r\n\r\n:::\r\n\r\n<br>\r\n\r\n**Discuss the results with your neighbor:**\r\n1) What did each of those changes do to the color of your HTML components? \r\n* What do you think that means for each of those values in the RGB code?\r\n",
    "bubble_choice_description": "Add RGB colors to a website.",
    "thumbnail_url": "https://images.code.org/3bac6caac33a537914df55d840e8b345-image-1588269048057.44.47 AM.png",
