          "id": "1",
          "name": "index.html",
          "language": "html",
          "contents": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n  <head>\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\">\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <!-- Info on RGB color -->\n    <h1>What is RGB Color?</h1>\n    \n    <p>The RGB color system is one of the most well-known color systems in the world. It combines red, green, and blue light to create the colors we see on our TV screens, computer monitors, and smartphones!</p>\n    \n    <h3>How Do You Use RGB Color?</h3>\n    \n    <p>Each color channel (red, green, and blue) is expressed from 0 (dull) to 255 (bright).</p>\n    \n    <p>This means that you can make 16,777,216 different colors when using RGB color!</p> \n  </body>\n</html>",
          "active": false,
          "folderId": "0"
        },
        "2": {
          "id": "2",
          "name": "style.css",
          "language": "css",
          "contents": "/* 1) Find the rule-set that gives the h1 tag its style. Change ONLY the first 0 to 255 */\n/* 2) Find the rule-set that gives the p tag its style. Change ONLY the second 0 to 255 */\n/* 3) Find the rule-set that gives the h3 tag its style. Change ONLY the third 0 to 255 */\n\nbody {\n  background: white;\n}\n\nh1{\n  color: rgb( 0 , 0, 0);\n}\n  h3 {\n  color: rgb( 0 , 0 , 0);\n}\n  p {\n  color: rgb( 0 , 0, 0);\n  }",
